    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2SVVBwzudQPmDfSxxJFg1z7)_\n\n## Merge order\n\n- Based on `main` (e8e60bee); independent of every other open PR.\n- No open PR registers a new `vulpea-ui` widget right now (checked the list). The view reads the `vulpea-ui` widget registry on every render, so widgets from the PR you are developing show up in it with no change here, whichever of the two merges first.\n- Touches `sp-vulpea.org` (new part before `sp-vulpea-org-ql.el`, plus the intro table) and `sp-vulpea-ui.el` (one `require` at the end). A text conflict is possible only with another PR editing those spots: keep both sides.\n- If merged out of order: nothing breaks.\n- After merging: restart Emacs (or `M-x sp-reload-modules`); nothing to retarget.\n\n## Summary\n\n- **Request:** show the backlinks and the other `vulpea-ui` widgets in a buffer apart from the sidebar, so a tiling window manager (AeroSpace, i3, sway) can place it in a frame of its own.\n- **New module** `sp-vulpea-ui-view` (`libraries/modules/vulpea/`), documented in `sp-vulpea.org` as a bullet-point part.\n  - `M-o v` (`sp-vulpea-ui-view-toggle`) opens the view in a new frame named `vulpea-ui-view` and closes it again. `q` closes, `g` refreshes. No `C-z/C-c/C-x/C-v` root, no Cmd+Space or Ctrl+Space; GUI only.\n  - It mounts `vulpea-ui-sidebar-root`, the sidebar's own root component, in its own buffer. So the view shows the same widgets in the same order: backlinks, grouped backlinks, see-also, concept usage, Link inbox, book position, and whatever is registered later.\n  - It follows the most recently used window that shows a vulpea note, in any frame. It keeps the last note while a non-note buffer is selected.\n  - It refreshes while idle and drops the caches when the note database changes, like the sidebar.\n  - A click in the view opens the note in the note window, not in the view (an `:around` advice on `vulpea-ui--get-main-window`), and focuses that frame.\n  - Settings (group `sp-vulpea-ui-view`): `use-frame` (nil shows it in a window of the current frame), `frame-name`, `frame-parameters`, `return-focus`, `focus-on-visit`.\n- **AeroSpace:** a suggested `[[on-window-detected]]` rule for the frame title is in `aerospace.org` as a doc note (`:tangle no`; `aerospace.toml` is unchanged). It is only needed if the frame floats.\n- **Relies on `vulpea-ui` internals** (`vulpea-ui-sidebar-root`, `vulpea-ui--get-note-from-buffer`, `vulpea-ui--get-main-window`, four jump functions); the doc lists them.\n- Tests: `tests/sp-vulpea-ui-view-test.el`, 10 ERT tests pass on Emacs 29.3 batch (followed note, sync and render kinds, main-window advice, focus advice, frame name, toggle and teardown). `.el` and test re-tangled from the doc; `when-let*` only, no CHANGELOG edit.\n- **Not tested with real `vulpea-ui`/`vui`, or a real second frame:** both are stubbed, and headless Emacs cannot make a frame. Please try it on the Mac.\n\n## Manual testing\n\nMac, `~/.config/emacs-modular`, with an Org note that has backlinks.\n\n- [x] Check out: `cd ~/dotfiles; git fetch origin 447-vulpea-ui-view-frame; git checkout 447-vulpea-ui-view-frame`, restart Emacs (or `M-x sp-reload-modules`)\n- [x] Unit tests: `cd ~/.config/emacs-modular; emacs -Q --batch -l tests/sp-vulpea-ui-view-test.el -f ert-run-tests-batch-and-exit` → 10 pass\n- [x] In a note, `M-o v`: a new frame named `vulpea-ui-view` opens with the backlinks and the other widgets; typing continues in the note frame\n- [x] AeroSpace tiles the new frame (if it floats, add the rule from `aerospace.org`, `aerospace reload-config`)\n- [x] Switch to another note (another window or frame): the view follows within a moment\n- [x] Select a non-note buffer: the view keeps the last note\n- [x] Open the sidebar too (`C-x t s`): both show the same widgets; the sidebar is unaffected\n- [x] Click a backlink in the view: the note opens in the note frame (not in the view) and that frame gets the focus\n- [x] `TAB`/widget toggling works in the view; `g` refreshes; edit a note, save, and the view updates\n- [ ] Widgets of the other in-development PR appear in the view without a change here\n- [x] `q` (or `M-o v` again) closes the view and its frame\n- [x] Set `sp-vulpea-ui-view-use-frame` to nil, `M-o v`: the view opens in a window of the current frame\n- [x] Regression: sidebar open/close and the Link inbox widget still work\n\n<details><summary>Revert after testing</summary>\n\n- Close the view: `M-o v` (or `q` in it).\n- Discard local edits: `git -C ~/dotfiles status`, then `git -C ~/dotfiles restore .`.\n- Back to main: `git -C ~/dotfiles switch main`, then `git -C ~/dotfiles pull`; restart Emacs (or `M-x sp-reload-modules`).\n- Fish shell works for all of the above; no yadm steps.\n\n</details>\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiCkP7qPMHnctiyKTgJ)_",
